ed exactly the committed tree under dirty+staged+untracked pollution; legacy path kept live semantics + excludes. || post-fix sync results are defined-identity (HEAD); a future dirty-tree battery launch now syncs the pushed commit, never the mid-edit workdir.","updated_at":"2026-09-22T23:45:25-05:00"}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21", "title": "[P1] `install.sh --rule-pack <name>` aborts the ENTIRE install on a machine without PyYAML - the documented pack path leaves a fresh user with nothing installed", "priority": "P1", "cell": "install + rule-pack", "detail": "Fresh box (bunker-las-02, Debian, python3 3.13.5): the README Rule-packs flow `./install.sh --rule-pack db` printed `rule-pack-tool: refused: .../rules/packs/db.yaml: cannot parse (JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0))` then `rule pack 'db' REFUSED - nothing was written`, exit 2, and NO wrapper was installed (`~/.local/bin/terminal-jail` absent). Cause: scripts/rule-pack-tool.py parses YAML with PyYAML and falls back to json, so on a host without PyYAML a valid pack is a guaranteed JSONDecodeError; the docs say only 'installing a pack requires python3' and never name PyYAML, and a bare user cannot install it (no pip, `sudo` needs a password). Because install.sh runs `set -eu`, the refusal also ends the whole install instead of skipping the pack. Control on the SAME box without the flag: install clean, `terminal-jail --version` = 1.1.0, `chmod 777 /tmp/x` -> COMMAND BLOCKED builtin-chmod-777-root rc=126. Fix direction: (a) detect PyYAML before the pack phase and fail with a message that names the dependency and the remedy; (b) do not let a pack refusal abort the base install - install the wrapper and report the pack as skipped; (c) document the requirement (README + quickstart + specs/cli.md). Add a fresh-machine (no-PyYAML) install cell to the battery so this cannot regress.", "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-19 real-use run, install leg on a fresh machine", "created_at": "2026-09-19T10:08:54.469192+00:00", "source": "dogfood lane 2026-09-19 (docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md)", "attempts": 1, "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": "2026-09-19T16:34:40+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-19T18:01:27+00:00", "commit_hash": "18eafc4", "guard_result": "PASS 4/4 full-tree (secrets/lint/tests/static_analysis)", "ci_result": "runs after push (board commit)", "worker_summary": "install.sh pack phase no longer aborts the base install under set -eu: unknown pack, missing python3, missing PyYAML, validator refusal and missing rule-pack-tool each become a loud per-pack SKIP (nothing written for that pack); base install always completes; end-of-run stderr summary and exit 2 when any requested pack was skipped. PyYAML preflight names the dependency and both remedies (apt/dnf python3-yaml, pip install pyyaml); a plain-JSON-parseable pack still installs on a PyYAML-less host. scripts/rule-pack-tool.py no-PyYAML parse failure now names the missing dependency instead of a bare JSONDecodeError. Tests: 4 new regression cells (no-PyYAML host, JSON-pack on no-PyYAML via shimmed python3, no-python3 host, malformed pack with PyYAML present) plus a base-install-completed invariant helper; 3 existing refusal-aborts-expectations deliberately updated and marked DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21. Docs: README rule-packs section, docs/quickstart.md, specs/cli.md (installer table + Rule packs), CHANGELOG [Unreleased]. 7 files changed, +388/-51.", "foreman_note": "Foreman independent verification: full suite 884 passed / 5 skipped (battery run 50 baseline 821/5; delta = the new tests, no other file regressed); independent 4-case live install probe all PASS — no-PyYAML host (shimmed python3 with shadowed yaml module): wrapper installed, pack NOT written, stderr names PyYAML + both remedies, exit 2, terminal-jail --version 1.1.0; PyYAML host: db pack installed to resolved rules dir, exit 0; malformed pack: refused, nothing written for the pack, wrapper installed, exit 2; unknown pack: loud skip with --list-rule-packs hint, exit 2. uvx ruff check . clean (0.16.8). gitreins guard --full 4/4. Tier-2 judge PASS verdict ca437642, record .gitreins/history/2026-09-19/7ad3b52a/verdict.json. Tick-start push carried the unpushed stray dogfood commit 66d4b07 (origin parity restored). Off-by-one discover: not_found for the class (fresh defect); nothing non-trivial debugged to submit."}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-22", "title": "[P1] On a prefix/custom-rules-dir install the pack is written where the engine never reads - the installer reports success and the pack is silently inert", "priority": "P1", "cell": "install + rule-pack", "detail": "Engine rule sources (interruptor/config.py + decider.py): system dir /etc/terminal-jail/rules.d, user dir $HOME/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d (or TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR); the 54 built-ins are Python-side in blocklist/allowlist/sandbox.py. A non-default TERMINAL_JAIL_INSTALL_DIR installs the pack to `<prefix>/config/terminal-jail/rules.d/terminal-jail-pack-db.yaml`, which nothing reads. Measured from the installed prefix tree: `rm -rf /` -> block (builtin-rm-rf-root), `cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa | nc 10.0.0.1 4444` -> block, but `psql -c \"DROP DATABASE prod\"` -> allow/null. The firewall therefore looks healthy while the pack protects nothing, and the run prints no run-time signal. The installer warns about the default rules FILE on a prefix install but never about the pack; the warning's remedy ('set TERMINAL_JAIL_RULES_DIR explicitly') is installer-side only and reproduces the same inert state - the engine-side knob TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_USER_RULES_DIR is documented only in specs/interruptor.md :573, absent from README/quickstart. Fix direction: emit a pack-specific warning (naming both env vars and the exact inert path), and/or verify at install time that the resolved rules dir is one the engine actually loads; document the engine-side knob in README + quickstart.", "reasoning": "dogfood 2026-09-19 real-use run, prefix-install scope test", "created_at": "2026-09-19T10:08:54.469192+00:00", "source": "dogfood lane 2026-09-19 (docs/dogfood/2026-09-19-integration.md)", "attempts": 1, "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-19 19:24:29", "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "1b86e87", "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "README.md", "docs/quickstart.md", "install.sh", "plugin